## Final Judgement
Based on the recorded evidence, the key findings are that a Miami Police Department officer, Daniel Ubeda, was photographed in uniform wearing a Trump 2020 mask at a Government Center polling location in Miami on October 20, 2020. Authorized officials, including the Miami Mayor and Police Chief, publicly condemned the action, stating it violated department and polling place policies and that the matter was "being addressed immediately" with the officer "facing discipline."

The evidence clearly establishes the incident and the official condemnation, but it does not provide any information confirming that formal disciplinary action was ultimately carried out or finalized. The sources note the department declined to comment on the specific punishment.

Therefore, while the claim that the officer would "face disciplinary action" is strongly supported by the officials' statements of intent, the fact-check record lacks the final confirmation needed to verify the outcome. The absence of evidence about the completed action does not prove it didn't happen, but it means the claim remains unverified.

`not enough information`

### Verdict: NEI

### Justification
Fact-checking confirmed that a Miami Police Department officer, Daniel Ubeda, was photographed in uniform wearing a Trump 2020 mask at a Government Center polling location in Miami on October 20, 2020, as reported by [ClickOrlando](https://www.clickorlando.com/news/florida/2020/10/20/florida-officer-to-be-disciplined-after-wearing-trump-mask-while-voting/) and [USA Today](https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/politics/elections/2020/10/20/miami-police-officer-trump-2020-mask-poll-discipline/6001128002/). Authorized officials, including Miami Mayor Francis Suarez and Police Chief Jorge Colina, publicly condemned the action, stating it violated department and polling place policies and that the matter was "being addressed immediately," with the officer "facing discipline" as noted by [The Ledger](https://www.theledger.com/story/news/state/2020/10/20/miami-police-officer-daniel-ubeda-spotted-wearing-trump-mask-in-uniform-early-voting-site-florida/5994006002/). However, the record provides no information confirming that formal disciplinary action was ultimately carried out or finalized, as the police department declined to comment on the specific punishment, leading to a verdict of `not enough information` to verify the claim's outcome.